*** Add File: CONTRIBUTING.md
+# Contributing to seasar2
+
+Thank you for considering contributing to this project! This document provides a short guide to help you get started.
+
+## Code of Conduct
+
+By participating in this project you agree to abide by the project's Code of Conduct. See CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md for details.
+
+## Getting the code
+
+Clone the repository and switch to the default branch:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/kkkkong/seasar2.git
+cd seasar2
+git checkout master
+```
+
+Or work from your fork/branch as preferred.
+
+## Build & Test (Maven)
+
+This repository uses Maven as its build tool. To build the project run:
+
+```bash
+mvn -B -DskipTests=false package
+```
+
+To run tests:
+
+```bash
+mvn test
+```
+
+If you want to build without running tests (fast):
+
+```bash
+mvn -DskipTests package
+```
+
+## Development checklist
+
+Before opening a pull request, please ensure:
+
+- [ ] You have included or updated tests for your changes
+- [ ] Formatting and coding conventions are followed
+- [ ] All tests pass locally (mvn test)
+- [ ] You have added or updated documentation if applicable
+
+## Pull Requests
+
+- Create a branch for your changes (e.g., `feature/my-change`)
+- Open a pull request against `master` (or the default branch)
+- Use the provided PR template to describe your changes
+
+## Reporting issues
+
+Please use the issue template when filing bug reports or feature requests. Provide as much information as possible (steps to reproduce, environment, logs).
+
+## CI and checks
+
+We run a Maven CI workflow that builds the project and runs tests on Linux across supported Java versions. If your change requires extra checks (linters, code formatters), please document them in CONTRIBUTING.md or add CI steps as part of your PR.
+
+## Contact
+
+If you need to reach the maintainers, see CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md for the contact placeholder.
+
